      "source_id": "journal-nature",
      "title": "SAMPLE: Reading a sealed Herculaneum scroll with machine learning",
      "abstract": "SAMPLE page, invented for tests and never fetched. Hundreds of papyrus scrolls from the library at Herculaneum were charred by the eruption of Mount Vesuvius in AD 79 and cannot be unrolled. We scanned one sealed scroll with X-rays and flattened its layers in software. We trained a machine-learning model to detect ink. The model was trained on small patches where ink had been found by hand. We read about 1,800 Greek letters in six columns of text. Scholars in two countries, outside our group, checked the readings. The text is a prose work on friendship. Open access. This article is licensed under a Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License. DOI 10.1038/nature-ut-sample-0001.",
